      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Express $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡5x$ in terms of $e$ using the definition of the hyperbolic sine.\n\n$\\operatorname{sinh}⁡5x=$\n {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}⁡5x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{5x}-{e}^{-5x}).\n$$",
