    "q-95492": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95492",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Given that $z>0,$ which of the following is equivalent to $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡z)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡z) & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}-{e}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{z}^{2}}-{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{z}^{-2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({z}^{2}-{z}^{-2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({z}^{2}-\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{{z}^{4}-1}{{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{z}^{4}-1}{2{z}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
