      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Evaluate $sinh\\,(\\frac{3}{2}).$ **Do not round** your answer.\n\n$\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{3/2}\\,-$ {{field-1}} $)$",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sinh\\,(\\frac{3}{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{3/2}-{e}^{-3/2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
