    "q-342675": {
      "dom_id": "step-q342675",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Simplify $\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(2q)$ in terms of $e$ using the definition of the hyperbolic tangent.\n\n$\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(2q)=$\n\n| {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n| ${e}^{4q}+1$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x & =\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}-1}{{e}^{2x}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-2x}}{1+{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the second definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(2q) & =\\frac{{e}^{2(2q)}-1}{{e}^{2(2q)}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4q}-1}{{e}^{4q}+1}\\,\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
