    "q-95601": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95601",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "$\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})=$",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x & =\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}-1}{{e}^{2x}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-2x}}{1+{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the third definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2}) & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-2(-1/2)}}{1+{e}^{-2(-1/2)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-e}{1+e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-95601-a",
