    "q-342677": {
      "dom_id": "step-q342677",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Simplify $tanh\\,(\\frac{k}{3})$ in terms of $e$ using the definition of the hyperbolic tangent.\n\n$tanh\\,(\\frac{k}{3})=$\n\n| {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n| ${e}^{2k/3}+1$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x & =\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}-1}{{e}^{2x}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-2x}}{1+{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the second definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tanh\\,(\\frac{k}{3}) & =\\frac{{e}^{2(k/3)}-1}{{e}^{2(k/3)}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2k/3}-1}{{e}^{2k/3}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
