    "q-342673": {
      "dom_id": "step-q342673",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Simplify $tanh\\,(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)$ using the definition of the hyperbolic tangent.\n\n$tanh\\,(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=$\n\n| {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n| ${x}^{3}+1$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x & =\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}-1}{{e}^{2x}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-2x}}{1+{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the second definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tanh\\,(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) & =\\frac{{e}^{2(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}-1}{{e}^{2(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}-1}{{e}^{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{3}}-1}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{3}}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}-1}{{x}^{3}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
